{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733974",
      "title": "Returning Responses in loader()s",
      "sourceHash": "7377e543192367dbfc0e46fa5c7a88203fc83dbf08fb9f1f704c471173983d9a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 5.52,
          "en": "Now I wanna dive back into the loader here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.52,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "It's an important feature of React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 11.46,
          "en": "and when using React Router you will use loaders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.46,
          "end": 13.89,
          "en": "and another feature we'll dive in later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.89,
          "end": 15.93,
          "en": "for fetching and sending data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.93,
          "end": 18.24,
          "en": "So it's important to understand this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.24,
          "end": 21.27,
          "en": "Now, one important aspect of a loader is to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.27,
          "end": 25.17,
          "en": "that you can return any kind of data in that loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.17,
          "end": 28.68,
          "en": "Here, I'm returning this events property, or the values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.68,
          "end": 31.38,
          "en": "stored in the events property of my response data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.38,
          "end": 32.34,
          "en": "and in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.34,
          "end": 34.743,
          "en": "it will actually be an array that I return.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 40.38,
          "en": "But we could return a number, some text, an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.38,
          "end": 41.7,
          "en": "whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.7,
          "end": 46.2,
          "en": "And what you can also return is a response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.2,
          "end": 48.57,
          "en": "Now what do I mean by that though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.57,
          "end": 53.01,
          "en": "Well, in the browser you can create a new response object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.01,
          "end": 54.42,
          "en": "which I'll name res, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.42,
          "end": 58.863,
          "en": "by instantiating the built-in response constructor function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.82,
          "end": 61.59,
          "en": "Now this is built into the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.59,
          "end": 63.63,
          "en": "This is a modern browser feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.63,
          "end": 66.15,
          "en": "You can build your own responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.15,
          "end": 69.09,
          "en": "and what's really important to understand at this point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.09,
          "end": 73.2,
          "en": "is that this loader code will not execute on a server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.2,
          "end": 77.07,
          "en": "This is still all happening in the browser here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.07,
          "end": 78.72,
          "en": "even though it's not in a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.72,
          "end": 80.64,
          "en": "it's still in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 82.83,
          "en": "This is still client-side code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.83,
          "end": 84.063,
          "en": "That's really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.05,
          "end": 87.45,
          "en": "Nonetheless, we can create a response here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 87.45,
          "end": 89.34,
          "en": "because the browser supports",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.34,
          "end": 92.10300000000001,
          "en": "this response constructor and response object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 95.07,
          "en": "Now, this response constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.07,
          "end": 99.47999999999999,
          "en": "also takes any data of your choice as a first argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.47999999999999,
          "end": 102.53999999999999,
          "en": "and then you can configure it with greater detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.53999999999999,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "with help of an extra object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 106.77000000000001,
          "en": "that can be set as a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 107.94,
          "en": "For example, you could set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.94,
          "end": 110.793,
          "en": "the status code of your response here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.83,
          "end": 117.12,
          "en": "Now, whenever you return such a response in your loaders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.12,
          "end": 119.75999999999999,
          "en": "the React Router package will automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 119.75999999999999,
          "end": 122.28,
          "en": "extract the data from your response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.28,
          "end": 124.74,
          "en": "when using useLoaderData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 124.74,
          "end": 127.47,
          "en": "So the data returned by useLoaderData",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 127.47,
          "end": 129.78,
          "en": "will still be the response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.78,
          "end": 133.71,
          "en": "that was part of the response you returned in your loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.71,
          "end": 135.81,
          "en": "Now, that might not seem too useful here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 135.81,
          "end": 139.65,
          "en": "because why would we create a separate response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.65,
          "end": 143.13,
          "en": "if we can just return the data like this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.13,
          "end": 145.32,
          "en": "This is way shorter, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.32,
          "end": 149.16,
          "en": "Well, yes it is, but this feature exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.16,
          "end": 152.16,
          "en": "because it's quite common that in this loader function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.16,
          "end": 153.81,
          "en": "you reach out to some backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.81,
          "end": 157.2,
          "en": "with the browser's built-in fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.2,
          "end": 159.03,
          "en": "And this fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.03,
          "end": 164.03,
          "en": "actually returns a promise that resolves to a response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 168.24,
          "en": "Now, combined with React Router's support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.24,
          "end": 170.28,
          "en": "for these response objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.28,
          "end": 173.01,
          "en": "and its automatic data extraction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.01,
          "end": 177.03,
          "en": "that simply means that you can, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "take that response, which you get here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 183.39,
          "en": "so this response object, and return that in your loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.39,
          "end": 185.76,
          "en": "You don't need to manually extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.76,
          "end": 187.41,
          "en": "the data from the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 187.41,
          "end": 191.4,
          "en": "Instead, you can return your response like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.4,
          "end": 194.46,
          "en": "with or without checking whether it's okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.46,
          "end": 195.39,
          "en": "that is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.39,
          "end": 198.483,
          "en": "and I'll get back to error handling in a couple of minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 199.5,
          "end": 202.17000000000002,
          "en": "But we can just return the response like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 202.17000000000002,
          "end": 203.57999999999998,
          "en": "and useLoaderData will then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.57999999999998,
          "end": 206.583,
          "en": "automatically give us the data that's part of the response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 207.51,
          "end": 211.11,
          "en": "Now, I just have to make sure that I do extract my events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 211.11,
          "end": 214.89,
          "en": "from that data object which I get here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.89,
          "end": 217.8,
          "en": "because that is actually an object with an events key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.8,
          "end": 220.89,
          "en": "just as I extracted events from the response data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 220.89,
          "end": 223.023,
          "en": "in my loader a couple of seconds ago.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 223.95,
          "end": 227.01,
          "en": "But with that, we can reduce our loader code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 227.01,
          "end": 230.22,
          "en": "and leverage this built-in support for response objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.22,
          "end": 233.16,
          "en": "And that's why I also wanted to mention that this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 233.16,
          "end": 237.27,
          "en": "special kind of return object is supported by React Router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 237.27,
          "end": 239.103,
          "en": "and its loader functions.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}